<ontology/use_pharmaceuticals/use_pharmaceuticals__doc_nux_vomica__q2/#resource> dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (2nd ed., 1840; Project Gutenberg #44562), s.v. STRYCHNIA" ;
    dcterms:source <https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/44562> ;
    a <ontology/EvidenceQuote/#resource> ;
    rdfs:label "Evidence for Nux Vomica used in Pharmaceuticals & Druggists' Preparations: Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (2nd ed., 1840; Project Gutenberg #44562), s.v. STRYCHNIA"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "STRYCHNIA, is an alkaline base, extracted from the Strychnos nux vomica, Strychnos ignatia, and the Upas tiente; which has been employed in medicine by some of the poison doctors, but is of no use in any of the arts."@en ;
